      "standardized_narrative": "At 31 December 2019 the syndicate identified adverse development on prior-year claims, with the managing agent noting a net deterioration (net) of GBP 8.4m to prior year reserves, principally driven by unfavourable developments in Property, Third party liability and Accident & Health, together with large market losses and a strengthening of tail assumptions in Non-Marine. Natural catastrophe activity in 2019 (notably Hurricane Dorian and Typhoon Hagibis) and the continuing impact of 2018 catastrophes (Hurricanes Michael and Florence and Californian wildfires) materially influenced reserve movements, partially offset by favourable developments across Energy, Marine and Political Risks.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "Included within net claims incurred of GBP 302.5m (2018: GBP 193.5m) is a deterioration of GBP 8.4m (2018: improvement of GBP 9.6m) to claims reserves established at the prior year end principally due to unfavourable developments on Property, Third party liability, Accident and Health Energy and Marine classes with partially offsetting favourable developments across the Energy, Marine and Political Risks accounts.",
        "The Property Binder account had material exposure to Hurricane Dorian which devastated the Bahamas during the third quarter as well as incurring strengthening to reserves in relation to 2018 events - Hurricanes Michael and Florence and Californian Wildfires. The Contingency account was also impacted the by 2019 natural catastrophes including Typhoon Hagibis. The Aviation and Space, Inwards Reinsurance and Specie accounts were impacted by some notable large market losses during the period, whilst the Non-Marine account saw an increase in the number of large losses reported and a strengthening to tail assumptions. There were partially offsetting improvements across the Energy, Marine and Political Risks accounts."
